        "cur->buf"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "same_object",
        "left": "cur->buf",
        "right": "cur->buf",
        "description": "Source identity relation for the vulnerability-relevant value."
      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "The first attacker-controlled GeneralName inside the SubjectAltName extension is materialized into the head `subject_alt_name` node. That makes `cur->buf.p` non-NULL, which is the state the next loop iteration uses to allocate `subject_alt_name->next` and later store the malformed tail entry."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_subject_alt_tail_must_be_cleared_after_error_cleanup",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "library/x509_crt.c",
      "function": "x509_get_subject_alt_name",
      "line": 684,
      "operands": [
        "NULL",
        "subject_alt_name->next"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "NULL",
        "right": "subject_alt_name->next"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_root_subject_alt_next_cleared_after_cleanup",
      "fine_trace_step": 7,
      "description": "After the malformed-entry cleanup frees every node reachable from `subject_alt_name->next`, the function returns the fatal SAN-parse error immediately without clearing `subject_alt_name->next`. The head sequence therefore keeps a dangling pointer while the same `ret` drives caller cleanup into `mbedtls_x509_crt_free`. The patch fixes this by inserting `subject_alt_name->next = NULL;` before the return."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_crt_free_reads_stale_subject_alt_tail",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "library/x509_crt.c",
      "function": "mbedtls_x509_crt_free",
      "line": 3280,
      "operands": [
        "seq_cur"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "seq_cur",
        "right": "seq_cur"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_crt_cleanup_tail_ptr_reaches_free_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 10,
      "description": "Certificate cleanup dereferences `seq_cur->next` on the already freed `subject_alt_names.next` node. AddressSanitizer reports this read as the crashing heap-use-after-free READ 8 in `mbedtls_x509_crt_free`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_crt_cleanup_reloads_dangling_subject_alt_tail",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_error_cleanup_tail_ptr_reused_by_crt_cleanup",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "library/x509_crt.c",
      "function": "mbedtls_x509_crt_free",
      "line": 3276,
      "fine_trace_step": 9,
      "state": "`mbedtls_x509_crt_free()` reloads `seq_cur` from `cert_cur->subject_alt_names.next`, and on the crashing path that field still holds the dangling tail pointer left by the earlier SAN cleanup.",
      "operands": [
        "seq_cur",
        "subject_alt_name->next"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "seq_cur",
        "right": "subject_alt_name->next"
      }
    }
